From ae7cb67308a7de1929b488a0adc2451046f70c1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viorel Cernateanu <vrilutza@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 19:22:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] spa: v4l2: keep the media type of the filter when it does not
 name a format

enum_filter_format() returns -ENOENT when the filter constrains the media type
but not the pixel format, for instance video/x-raw with no format field. The
caller then falls back to plain VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT, which walks every pixel format
of the device, and nothing checks the media type again: the param handed back
can carry a media subtype the filter excluded.

On a UVC camera that enumerates MJPG before YUYV, a client asking for raw
640x480 is given image/jpeg 640x480. pipewiresrc intersects that with what it
asked for, gets empty caps and fails with "error use input buffers: -22"; the
stream never starts.

Apply the filter's media type and subtype on that path as well. A filter that
names a pixel format never reaches this code and is unaffected, and without a
filter nothing changes.

diff --git a/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c b/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c
index c85d6fff1..2a8ee4043 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c
@@ -759,6 +759,18 @@ do_enum_fmt:
 						this->props.device);
 				goto exit;
 			}
+			/* This enumerates every pixel format of the device, so a
+			 * filter that constrains the media type but not the pixel
+			 * format is only applied here. */
+			if (filter) {
+				const struct format_info *fi =
+					fourcc_to_format_info(port->fmtdesc.pixelformat);
+
+				if (fi == NULL ||
+				    fi->media_type != filter_media_type ||
+				    fi->media_subtype != filter_media_subtype)
+					goto next_fmtdesc;
+			}
 		}
 		port->next_fmtdesc = false;
 		port->frmsize.index = 0;

